      "x": 360,
      "y": 1320
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 217,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`HTMLToken.svelte:17` computes `html = DOMPurify.sanitize(token.text)`, but the iframe / `<file>` / `<status>` / `<source_id>` branches (lines 55, 72, 87, 105, 123) test raw `token.text` on purpose."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 218,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "DOMPurify's stock profile removes `<iframe>` with its contents (`ALLOWED_TAGS` omits it, `DEFAULT_FORBID_CONTENTS` includes it) and erases the four custom tags (no hyphen, so the custom-element regex rejects them)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 219,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The invariant: every raw-text branch either pins its origin or renders with bare `sandbox` (the generic branch, whose `src` is unvalidated)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 220,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "YouTube hardcodes `youtube.com/embed/` + an 11-char id regex; file uses a same-origin admin-gated endpoint."
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 221,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "One comment at line 17 stating why `html` is only for `<video>`/`<audio>`. Done 2026-11-02."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 222,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`scripts/gates/` check on the `startr-swap/check.py` `--check`/`--self-test` shape, keyed on the `src={iframeSrc}` binding (not a line number). ~60 lines, belongs in `gauntlet_fast`."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 223,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Assert the generic branch keeps bare `sandbox` and `allow-scripts`+`allow-same-origin` never co-occur."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 224,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Trap for the fixer: the line-82 `onload` autosizer is already broken under bare sandbox (opaque-origin `SecurityError`) \u2014 exactly the \"just make the height work\" bait that weakens the sandbox."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 225,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Coverage is zero: grep of all 46 Cypress specs for `sandbox|iframe|HTMLToken` returns nothing."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 226,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "If the app-pane work lands first, add the line-73 origin allowlist BEFORE gating, so the gate does not freeze a `sandbox` we mean to change."
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "9d1df1f82358011b",
      "line_num": 216,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**HTMLToken raw-text invariant \u2014 document and gate it, do NOT \"fix\" the asymmetry (Note 2 of the 2026-08-15 poka-yoke resolution): branching on `html` silently breaks five features, not three. #security #bonsai ([dossier](docs/board-dossiers.md))**\n- [ ] `HTMLToken.svelte:17` computes `html = DOMPurify.sanitize(token.text)`, but the iframe / `<file>` / `<status>` / `<source_id>` branches (lines 55, 72, 87, 105, 123) test raw `token.text` on purpose.\n- [ ] DOMPurify's stock profile removes `<iframe>` with its contents (`ALLOWED_TAGS` omits it, `DEFAULT_FORBID_CONTENTS` includes it) and erases the four custom tags (no hyphen, so the custom-element regex rejects them).\n- [ ] The invariant: every raw-text branch either pins its origin or renders with bare `sandbox` (the generic branch, whose `src` is unvalidated).\n- [ ] YouTube hardcodes `youtube.com/embed/` + an 11-char id regex; file uses a same-origin admin-gated endpoint.\n- [x] One comment at line 17 stating why `html` is only for `<video>`/`<audio>`. Done 2026-11-02.\n- [ ] `scripts/gates/` check on the `startr-swap/check.py` `--check`/`--self-test` shape, keyed on the `src={iframeSrc}` binding (not a line number). ~60 lines, belongs in `gauntlet_fast`.\n- [ ] Assert the generic branch keeps bare `sandbox` and `allow-scripts`+`allow-same-origin` never co-occur.\n- [ ] Trap for the fixer: the line-82 `onload` autosizer is already broken under bare sandbox (opaque-origin `SecurityError`) \u2014 exactly the \"just make the height work\" bait that weakens the sandbox.\n- [ ] Coverage is zero: grep of all 46 Cypress specs for `sandbox|iframe|HTMLToken` returns nothing.\n- [ ] If the app-pane work lands first, add the line-73 origin allowlist BEFORE gating, so the gate does not freeze a `sandbox` we mean to change.\n\n`TODO.md:L216`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 360,
      "y": 1410
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 237,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[WE] Plan it after the demo; interview Alexander first; plan file in `~/.claude/plans/`"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 238,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Decide first: AI-UI signs sessions with HS256 and `WEBUI_SECRET_KEY` (`utils/auth.py:38`), so any project that verifies them with that key can also mint a session for any user, admin included"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 239,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The likely answer: an OpenID Connect (OIDC) provider in AI-UI, one client per project, tokens signed with a private key whose public half (JWKS) is all a project holds"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 240,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Today AI-UI signs people in only as a client: OAuth/OIDC providers (`utils/oauth.py`), LDAP, and the trusted e-mail header (`WEBUI_AUTH_TRUSTED_EMAIL_HEADER`)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 241,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Consumers: Trellis (its card \"AI-UI is the identity provider\", decided 2026-09-17; personas on try.sage.is, amendment 44), the Tinker.Click library server (upstream; needs OIDC client support), community.sage.is"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 242,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Ties to the federation plan's \"identity across boxes\" flow, and its open question: how a box proves who it is"
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "481494cdc0c21976",
      "line_num": 236,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**AI-UI as the single sign-on for our other projects #auth #federation (Alexander, 2026-10-15; plan after the Brokerage H demo): one AI-UI login opens Trellis, the Tinker.Click library server and later projects, so no project keeps its own user list**\n- [ ] [WE] Plan it after the demo; interview Alexander first; plan file in `~/.claude/plans/`\n- [ ] Decide first: AI-UI signs sessions with HS256 and `WEBUI_SECRET_KEY` (`utils/auth.py:38`), so any project that verifies them with that key can also mint a session for any user, admin included\n- [ ] The likely answer: an OpenID Connect (OIDC) provider in AI-UI, one client per project, tokens signed with a private key whose public half (JWKS) is all a project holds\n- [ ] Today AI-UI signs people in only as a client: OAuth/OIDC providers (`utils/oauth.py`), LDAP, and the trusted e-mail header (`WEBUI_AUTH_TRUSTED_EMAIL_HEADER`)\n- [ ] Consumers: Trellis (its card \"AI-UI is the identity provider\", decided 2026-09-17; personas on try.sage.is, amendment 44), the Tinker.Click library server (upstream; needs OIDC client support), community.sage.is\n- [ ] Ties to the federation plan's \"identity across boxes\" flow, and its open question: how a box proves who it is\n\n`TODO.md:L236`",
