      "y": 2130
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 340,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Public commitment: the sage.is/bonsai FAQ says \"A Sprig marketplace is on our roadmap to make selling one simple\""
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 341,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Alexander (CTO) was a founding engineer at Etsy (employee #5), named on the page"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 342,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Methodology = Etsy for maker-simple selling + Shopify's developer playbook (partner program, first-class SDKs/docs \u2014 the MIT `sage-is-sprig-sdk-py` is the seed \u2014 builder-favoring revenue share)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 343,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Interacts with the in-house registry cutover \u2014 paid artifacts need authenticated pulls"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 344,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Interacts with catalog schema enrichment (license/tier/price)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 345,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Interacts with `delivery: service-endpoint` \u2014 hosted paid Sprigs need no artifact download"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 346,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Scope TBD: payments, publisher identity/verification, revenue split, how a purchase lands in an operator's catalog"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 347,
          "tags": [
            "#bonsai",
            "#marketplace"
          ],
          "text": "**Architecture approved 2026-07-19 (roadmap-only, no code yet)**: spine = catalog-as-data \u2014 a new source of entries, not a new trust model."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 348,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The one hard blocker is `SprigSupervisor.CATALOG`, a hardcoded Python dict (`supervisor.py` ~222-625)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 349,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Extract the `_sprig()` entry schema to a validated model; merge entries from three runtime sources into the unchanged graft pipeline (allowlist \u2192 arch guard \u2192 pull \u2192 sha256 \u2192 minisign \u2192 extract \u2192 spawn)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 350,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Three lanes = a trust ladder: S1 first-party curated signed index; S2 curated community, publisher-signed via the per-entry `pubkey`"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 351,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "S3 admin self-load: any OCI ref at runtime, volume-persisted, graftable with no image rebuild; `SPRIG_REQUIRE_SIGNED=1` ratchets an instance to signed-only"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 352,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Phase M1: catalog-as-data + admin self-load \u2014 also redacts `repo/tag/binary_sha256/insecure` from the browser catalog"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 353,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Phases M2-M5: M2 remote storefront + in-house registry cutover (Zot), M3 discovery UX, M4 community submission, M5 commerce"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 354,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Open: storefront name, M1 index shape, self-load sha-pin default, Zot vs GHCR-proxy, entitlement binding"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 355,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Design: memory `project_sprig_marketplace.md`"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 356,
          "tags": [
            "#bonsai",
            "#marketplace"
          ],
          "text": "**Quarter slice, scoped 2026-08-15 against a social push**: the push needs the store to exist."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 357,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "M1 stays at position 3 in the `#### Platform unlocks` sequence, so the push date depends on Spaces multi-user and spend budgets \u2014 book no announcement against a date those two control"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 358,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Ships: M1 catalog-as-data, M1b admin self-load (`POST \u2026/sprigs/load`, `sprigs.d/*.json` on the volume), `/catalog` redaction"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 359,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Ships: schema enrichment (`display_name`, `description`, `size_mb`, `license`, `tier`, `publisher`, `homepage` \u2014 once, with M1)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 360,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Ships: browse/search UI over the 20 shipped sprigs"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 361,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Should: remote signed `catalog.json` on a Sage.is URL, artifacts staying on GHCR"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 362,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Does not ship: public submission lane, storefront index, M5 commerce, in-house registry, `delivery: service-endpoint`"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 363,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Dropping the public lane defers signature liability \u2014 self-load is admin-only; the admin stays the trust boundary"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 364,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "We do not charge makers to list (present tense, not \"ever\"); creators earn through contracts we sell direct, not a storefront cut"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 365,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Cards: `charts/sprig-creator-program/TODO.md`"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 366,
          "tags": [
            "#security",
            "#critical"
          ],
          "text": "**Blocker \u2014 the `execute` event runs arbitrary JS in the top frame, and a listing policy does not fix it**."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 367,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`POST /api/v1/functions/load/url` (`routers/functions.py:82`) installs a `main.py` from any GitHub URL today, no marketplace involved"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 368,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "A push that brings thousands of self-installers widens that surface"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 369,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Pick one and record it for the endpoint: gate it or accept the risk in writing. The event half is closed: neutered 2026-11-02"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 370,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Keeping Functions out of the community lane is correct and cheap but is not the control"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 371,
          "tags": [
            "#security",
            "#critical"
          ],
          "text": "**Blocker \u2014 no CSP exists, and enforcing a fresh one the week before a launch breaks the product**: tracked on the **CSP-configured gate** card under Repo Hygiene & Security, whose children carry these facts (merged 2026-11-02)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 372,
          "tags": [
            "#bonsai"
          ],
          "text": "**The app pane is the store's actual product, and it is not built** \u2014 four gaps."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 373,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "An installed app must open like an Artifact, run, and report progress \u2014 not \"the assistant can call your API\"; `Artifacts.svelte` already supplies the pane"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 374,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The bridge validates by `event.origin`; a `srcdoc` frame without `allow-same-origin` has an opaque origin, so its postMessage arrives as `\"null\"` and is rejected at `Chat.svelte:416`"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 375,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Validate `event.source === iframeElement.contentWindow` instead"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 376,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Service workers, localStorage, IndexedDB, and Cache API need a real origin, so a genuine PWA cannot run in a `srcdoc` pane \u2014 in-container is the only rung where \"PWA-type app\" is literally true"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 377,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Student progress needs a per-user per-sprig state API on the rootstock, not browser storage"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 378,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "_2 done steps archived 2026-11-03 \u2192 docs/completed-todos.md._"
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "ec28715c691d9f80",
      "line_num": 339,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [
        "#bonsai",
        "#marketplace"
      ],
      "text": "**Sprig\u2122 marketplace \u2014 simple selling of Sprigs (captured 2026-07-08; now a PUBLIC commitment): support paid and proprietary Sprigs with selling as simple as Etsy made it for makers. ([dossier](docs/board-dossiers.md))**\n- [ ] Public commitment: the sage.is/bonsai FAQ says \"A Sprig marketplace is on our roadmap to make selling one simple\"\n- [ ] Alexander (CTO) was a founding engineer at Etsy (employee #5), named on the page\n- [ ] Methodology = Etsy for maker-simple selling + Shopify's developer playbook (partner program, first-class SDKs/docs \u2014 the MIT `sage-is-sprig-sdk-py` is the seed \u2014 builder-favoring revenue share)\n- [ ] Interacts with the in-house registry cutover \u2014 paid artifacts need authenticated pulls\n- [ ] Interacts with catalog schema enrichment (license/tier/price)\n- [ ] Interacts with `delivery: service-endpoint` \u2014 hosted paid Sprigs need no artifact download\n- [ ] Scope TBD: payments, publisher identity/verification, revenue split, how a purchase lands in an operator's catalog\n- [ ] **Architecture approved 2026-07-19 (roadmap-only, no code yet)**: spine = catalog-as-data \u2014 a new source of entries, not a new trust model. #bonsai #marketplace\n- [ ] The one hard blocker is `SprigSupervisor.CATALOG`, a hardcoded Python dict (`supervisor.py` ~222-625)\n- [ ] Extract the `_sprig()` entry schema to a validated model; merge entries from three runtime sources into the unchanged graft pipeline (allowlist \u2192 arch guard \u2192 pull \u2192 sha256 \u2192 minisign \u2192 extract \u2192 spawn)\n- [ ] Three lanes = a trust ladder: S1 first-party curated signed index; S2 curated community, publisher-signed via the per-entry `pubkey`\n- [ ] S3 admin self-load: any OCI ref at runtime, volume-persisted, graftable with no image rebuild; `SPRIG_REQUIRE_SIGNED=1` ratchets an instance to signed-only\n- [ ] Phase M1: catalog-as-data + admin self-load \u2014 also redacts `repo/tag/binary_sha256/insecure` from the browser catalog\n- [ ] Phases M2-M5: M2 remote storefront + in-house registry cutover (Zot), M3 discovery UX, M4 community submission, M5 commerce\n- [ ] Open: storefront name, M1 index shape, self-load sha-pin default, Zot vs GHCR-proxy, entitlement binding\n- [ ] Design: memory `project_sprig_marketplace.md`\n- [ ] **Quarter slice, scoped 2026-08-15 against a social push**: the push needs the store to exist. #bonsai #marketplace\n- [ ] M1 stays at position 3 in the `#### Platform unlocks` sequence, so the push date depends on Spaces multi-user and spend budgets \u2014 book no announcement against a date those two control\n- [ ] Ships: M1 catalog-as-data, M1b admin self-load (`POST \u2026/sprigs/load`, `sprigs.d/*.json` on the volume), `/catalog` redaction\n- [ ] Ships: schema enrichment (`display_name`, `description`, `size_mb`, `license`, `tier`, `publisher`, `homepage` \u2014 once, with M1)\n- [ ] Ships: browse/search UI over the 20 shipped sprigs\n- [ ] Should: remote signed `catalog.json` on a Sage.is URL, artifacts staying on GHCR\n- [ ] Does not ship: public submission lane, storefront index, M5 commerce, in-house registry, `delivery: service-endpoint`\n- [ ] Dropping the public lane defers signature liability \u2014 self-load is admin-only; the admin stays the trust boundary\n- [ ] We do not charge makers to list (present tense, not \"ever\"); creators earn through contracts we sell direct, not a storefront cut\n- [ ] Cards: `charts/sprig-creator-program/TODO.md`\n- [ ] **Blocker \u2014 the `execute` event runs arbitrary JS in the top frame, and a listing policy does not fix it**. #security #critical\n- [ ] `POST /api/v1/functions/load/url` (`routers/functions.py:82`) installs a `main.py` from any GitHub URL today, no marketplace involved\n- [ ] A push that brings thousands of self-installers widens that surface\n- [ ] Pick one and record it for the endpoint: gate it or accept the risk in writing. The event half is closed: neutered 2026-11-02\n- [ ] Keeping Functions out of the community lane is correct and cheap but is not the control\n- [ ] **Blocker \u2014 no CSP exists, and enforcing a fresh one the week before a launch breaks the product**: tracked on the **CSP-configured gate** card under Repo Hygiene & Security, whose children carry these facts (merged 2026-11-02). #security #critical\n- [ ] **The app pane is the store's actual product, and it is not built** \u2014 four gaps. #bonsai\n- [ ] An installed app must open like an Artifact, run, and report progress \u2014 not \"the assistant can call your API\"; `Artifacts.svelte` already supplies the pane\n- [ ] The bridge validates by `event.origin`; a `srcdoc` frame without `allow-same-origin` has an opaque origin, so its postMessage arrives as `\"null\"` and is rejected at `Chat.svelte:416`\n- [ ] Validate `event.source === iframeElement.contentWindow` instead\n- [ ] Service workers, localStorage, IndexedDB, and Cache API need a real origin, so a genuine PWA cannot run in a `srcdoc` pane \u2014 in-container is the only rung where \"PWA-type app\" is literally true\n- [ ] Student progress needs a per-user per-sprig state API on the rootstock, not browser storage\n- [x] _2 done steps archived 2026-11-03 \u2192 docs/completed-todos.md._\n\n`#bonsai` `#marketplace`\n`TODO.md:L339`",
