    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 442,
          "tags": [
            "#frontend",
            "#perf",
            "#critical"
          ],
          "text": "**SURVEYED: every migration candidate on one snapshot \u2014 the sorting key was wrong** (Alexander, 2026-08-02)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 443,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`cypress/e2e/upgrade/route-payload.cy.ts` 10/10 green on the restored snapshot (51 agents / 32 users / 17 knowledge bases / 8 prompts)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 444,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The floor: `/notes` with no data of its own costs 127 requests / 781 kB wire / 7,575 kB decoded"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 445,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Route deltas above it: prompts +121 kB, functions +206, users +296, knowledge +455, evaluations +1,269, agents +1,714, chat +5,170 \u2014 for six of eight routes the list is 2\u20136% of what loading it costs"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 446,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`/api/models` is 2,304 kB, fetched on every route, never cached: 741 of the 781 kB wire (95%) on a warm client"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 447,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Server-rendered comparison: 12 requests / 234 kB wire / 472 kB decoded \u2014 one sixteenth of the EMPTY SvelteKit route"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 448,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Method: decoded kB is the ranking column; wire kB is a returning-visitor figure (cold numbers in `workshop-payload.cy.ts`); `/home` not surveyed \u2014 Spaces has no list hook yet"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 449,
          "tags": [
            "#frontend"
          ],
          "text": "**Reorder on lines deleted and open frequency \u2014 throughput no longer breaks ties.**"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 450,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Component lines: users 3,126 \u00b7 notes 2,910 \u00b7 knowledge 1,671 \u00b7 evaluations 1,359 \u00b7 functions 1,249 \u00b7 prompts 635 (ceilings \u2014 Agents landed at 53% of its count)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 451,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "No telemetry exists, so the frequency column stays empty until Alexander fills it"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 452,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`/admin/users` moves ahead of knowledge: largest component, the one surface that actually renders its base64 avatars, `users.cy.ts` already guards it"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 453,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`/notes` is judged off this table: 2,910 lines of editor, not a list \u2014 the props-and-forms pattern may not apply"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 454,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`/workshop/prompts` as warm-up: 635 lines, +121 kB, an afternoon"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 455,
          "tags": [
            "#frontend",
            "#perf",
            "#critical"
          ],
          "text": "**THE FLOOR \u2014 parts 2 and 3: `/api/models` is the whole of what is left.**"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 456,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The floor stands at 6,642 kB; `/api/models` is 2,304 kB of it and never caches \u2014 741 kB over the wire on every navigation"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 457,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Fixing the floor helps every route in the product, including the ones the strangler never reaches"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 458,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Stop fetching `/api/models` on routes that never render it \u2014 it rides the `(app)` layout boot wave (`+layout.svelte:120`)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 459,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`/notes`, `/admin/users`, `/admin/functions`, `/admin/evaluations` each pay 2.3 MB for a model list they never render"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 460,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Shrink the payload: `utils/models.py:175` sets `model[\"info\"] = custom_model.model_dump()` per row, base64 avatars included \u2014 why it is 2,304 kB instead of tens of kB"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 461,
          "tags": [
            "#backend"
          ],
          "text": "**`routers/knowledge.py:42` writes to the database during a GET and queries once per row.**"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 462,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`get_knowledge` calls `Files.get_file_metadatas_by_ids` per knowledge base (the `Models.get_models()` N+1 shape) and prunes dead file ids via `update_knowledge_data_by_id`"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 463,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "So a concurrent read storm can write, and readers silently repair data"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 464,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Fix AS the knowledge migration, on the \"prune, don't port\" rule"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 465,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The no-build Prompts panel must not port the slash bug: it normalises on lookup"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 466,
          "tags": [
            "#frontend",
            "#perf",
            "#critical"
          ],
          "text": "**Workshop is the next surface, elevated on production numbers** (Alexander, 2026-08-01)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 467,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Worst surface in the product; the only one missing the throughput budget (\u2264 ~2 MB transferred, first content < 2 s) on every axis"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 468,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`/workshop/models` 144 requests / 20,520 kB / 6,181 kB transferred / 32 s"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 469,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`/workshop/knowledge` ~140 requests / 18,203 kB / 5,257 kB / 19.07 s \u2014 a LIST OF MODELS slower than the 172 req / 7.9 MB / ~19 s conversation baseline"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 470,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "5,567 lines across models/knowledge/prompts; the table predicts ~50\u201365%"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 471,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "First task is a before-measurement \u2014 the last two such assumptions (22 MB WASM, markdown libs) measured false"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 472,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Candidate, read not measured: serial waterfall \u2014 route awaits `getModels` before `<Models />`, which then fetches `getWorkshopModels` + `getGroups` + `getBranding`"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 473,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Candidate: static `marked`, `sortablejs`, `file-saver` in `Models.svelte`"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 474,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Candidate: static `fuse.js`, `dayjs` + `relativeTime` in `Knowledge.svelte`"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 475,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Candidate: base64 `model.meta.profile_image_url` per row"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 476,
          "tags": [
            "#frontend",
            "#perf",
            "#critical"
          ],
          "text": "**The list payload repeats the same owner avatar once per agent** (filed 2026-08-01, measured 2026-08-02; `cypress/e2e/upgrade/workshop-payload.cy.ts` on the snapshot)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 477,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`GET /api/v1/models/` nests the owner's whole `UserResponse` per row: 475 kB of base64 avatars the page never renders (rows show \"By {name}\" as text)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 478,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "21 of 32 users carry avatars, 120 kB amplified ~4\u00d7 by repetition"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 479,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`/api/models` 2,304 kB + `/api/v1/models/` 1,503 kB = 3,807 kB \u2014 41% of the page load, two endpoints carrying the same base64"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 480,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "SPA: 126 requests / 3,604 kB wire / 9,174 kB decoded / 5.4 s to first row; production's 20 MB does not fully reproduce (requests within 13%, bytes ~half)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 481,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Server-rendered: 11 requests / 234 kB / 152 ms cold, 7 kB / 44 ms repeat (0 data URIs vs 66; 6 cacheable avatar URLs)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 482,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "In-app arrival still costs 919 kB wire (914 kB is `/api/v1/models/`) and 1,504 ms to first row"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 483,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Timing stamped in-browser with `performance.now()` at the click, because `Date.now()` in a Cypress body stamps at queue time"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 484,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Like-for-like (server page 1 is 24 rows vs the SPA's 51, so count both pages): 22 requests / ~477 kB \u2014 7.6\u00d7 less wire, 5.7\u00d7 fewer requests"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 485,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Also: `Models.get_models()` calls `Users.get_user_by_id()` in its loop \u2014 49 queries for 48 rows"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 486,
          "tags": [
            "#frontend",
            "#perf"
          ],
          "text": "**A 166 kB favicon, a 166 kB splash and a 636 kB unsubsetted `Archivo-Variable.ttf` ride every cold page load** (found 2026-08-02 in the workshop top-25)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 487,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Reopens the `/icons/` \"not perf\" call (the \"already-gated\" card in this section), which judged the file on disk"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 488,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Just under 1 MB before anything renders, on the SPA and the server-rendered pages alike \u2014 PNG does not compress again on the wire, and a favicon is 16\u201348 px"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 489,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Cheap and separable from the migration: resize the icon set to the sizes actually declared"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 490,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Subset the font (the 2026-08-17 `sage-archivo.ttf` subsetting card under In Progress automated the build-time subset; re-measure what each page still loads)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 491,
          "tags": [
            "#frontend",
            "#perf"
          ],
          "text": "**Avatars: one right size at the encoder plus a serve-time cache behind a cacheable URL \u2014 30\u00d7 measured, no new dependency beyond Pillow** (DECIDED 2026-08-01, Alexander)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 492,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Decision: migration AND serve-time cache, not encoder-only \u2014 the migration's job is getting the blob out of the database row"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 493,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Three real 250\u00d7250 avatars: 106.8 / 97.7 / 95.0 kB as PNG, 21 kB as JPEG, 5.9\u20137.2 kB at 128 px, 3.6\u20134.5 kB at 88 px \u2014 format alone 5\u00d7, format-plus-size 30\u00d7"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 494,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Root cause: one canvas-resize block pasted three times (`ModelEditor.svelte:366`, `Settings/Account.svelte:134`, `ArenaModelModal.svelte:202`)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 495,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Only the agent copy omits the format argument, so it defaults to PNG"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 496,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "One shared encoder helper: WebP with JPEG fallback, dimensions matched to the slot"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 497,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Migration moves originals to content-addressed storage on the data volume, leaving a reference in the row"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 498,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Non-destructive (write, verify, then clear the row), idempotent, fails closed when the volume is not writable (`data_not_writable` issue_type)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 499,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Serve-time cache derives sizes beside the originals on first request; sizes come from a CLOSED set (44/128/256), never a free query parameter; cache on the volume, not in memory (multi-worker roadmap)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 500,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Exports must re-inline from storage and land WITH the migration \u2014 `Models.svelte:167` and `admin/Settings/Models.svelte:68` `JSON.stringify` models verbatim, so a local path silently breaks import portability"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 501,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Hardening: format allowlist, byte ceiling, `Image.MAX_IMAGE_PIXELS`; Pillow verified absent from `requirements.txt` and the built image"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 502,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Proof: `make upgrade_gate` boots a real snapshot"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 503,
          "tags": [
            "#frontend",
            "#brand"
          ],
          "text": "**Rename `/workshop/models` \u2192 `/workshop/agents`** (Alexander, 2026-08-01)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 504,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The UI already says Agents (`Models.svelte` heading, page title, Import/Export Agents); only the URL, directory and component names say models"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 505,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Consistent with the locked 2026-07-11 single tiered \"Agents\" surface decision"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 506,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Do it AS the migration \u2014 renaming twice costs two redirect layers"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 507,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The route, the nav label, the i18n keys, and a redirect from the old path for bookmarks"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 508,
          "tags": [
            "#biomes",
            "#ratchet"
          ],
          "text": "Count and pin the core biomes as a downward-only ratchet \u2014 chat core, rich-text editor, code editor, flow canvas, channels; the count only decreases"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 509,
          "tags": [
            "#frontend"
          ],
          "text": "**Mid-term: rebuild the chat core as a server-rendered fragment flow on startr-swap, not a ported island** (Alexander, 2026-07-27; \"htmx\" reworded 2026-11-02, since htmx leaves per the Remove htmx card)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 510,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The port is priced at 17,591 lines for a 15\u201330% cut"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 511,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Fragment-first has the server own the conversation and send fragments, only the token stream stays vanilla \u2014 Phase S proved that half in ~260 lines, abort semantics included"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 512,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "A hypothesis with two Phase 0 datapoints; do NOT re-plan the phase order until one fragment surface is migrated and measured"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 513,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The non-proxying browser driver Phase S made a condition"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 514,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "One migrated, measured fragment surface \u2014 the datum that settles it"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 515,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Reimplement the flow canvas (`@xyflow/svelte`) framework-free"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 516,
          "tags": [
            "#brand"
          ],
          "text": "Slogan precision: \"org-owned\" not \"user-owned\"; keep yjs local-first for the editor"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 517,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "_7 done steps archived 2026-11-03 \u2192 docs/completed-todos.md._"
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
