          "line_num": 51,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[MANUALLY] Release and deploy 3.3.0 by run sheet `Plans/ai-ui-3.3.0-release` (everything in the tree ships, decided 2026-11-05; gates green 2026-11-05); then the steps below"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 52,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[MANUALLY] Tell both box owners (the note says the hole \"is closed\")"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 53,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[MANUALLY] Rotate the backup remote's credentials (urgent half: plaintext nightly backups, the August cluster compromise) and `WEBUI_SECRET_KEY` (`PRIVACY_KEY` gets its own value first)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 54,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[MANUALLY] Bump the tap formula"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 56,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[WE] Then `docs/rootstock/design.md`; OpenAPI capture and goldens from the 3.2.1 image; the parity runner"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 57,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[WE] F1 (3.4.0): the seam, pass-through; the ten congestion fixes (card \"Congestion\" in Bugs); consistent backups; `make stream_load` with an asyncio mock provider"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 58,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[WE] F2 (3.5.0): the model gateway, a plain ASGI app in its own process, behind an nginx inside the container; the Workshop agents page on Django; WAL with its own switch; Alexander's go or no-go"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 59,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[WE] The gateway's byte path moves to Rust (Tinker's `core/src/llm`) only when `stream_load` shows a trigger: gateway CPU over 60% of a core, loop lag p99 over 50 ms, added first-token p95 over 50 ms, or more than 250 streams"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 60,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[WE] Image diet (decided 2026-10-23: Django squeezed, containers everywhere): 3.2.1 is 390 MB on disk (123\u2013126 MB to download); at F8 must \u2264150 MB, target \u2264110, stretch \u226475; `image_budget` ratchets down each release; levers measured in the plan (63 MB of `.pyc`, 37 MB `uv`, a doubled 21 MB zstandard, Django trimmed 49\u219224 MB)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 61,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[WE] Repo weight: 97 MB tracked against Tinker's 19, though the code is about the same size"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 62,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[MANUALLY] Create both repos in the `Sage.is` org: the agent's Gitea token has no `write:organization`, so creating an org repo answers 403"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 63,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[WE] Then upload the fonts and the `.xcf`, have the export-document recipe fetch the fonts by sha256, and drop all of them from git with a pointer note in `app/static/icons/`"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 64,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[WE] Few libraries (Alexander, 2026-10-23; evidence in the plan): `test_dependencies.py` lists about 12 direct Python packages, about 30 installed by their closure (today 95), no npm package at runtime (today 1,160 build the SPA), vendored pinned files checked by sha256, hash-pinned locks with an `exclude-newer` cool-down"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 65,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[WE] Install and onboarding: `install_smoke` times a fresh install to the first answer and counts the steps; it fails on any tour, modal or carousel before that answer"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 66,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[MANUALLY] SSO decision from the `federation/` research note, before F6, where sign-in now moves"
