      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "77ecdbe5a210a3a6",
      "line_num": 651,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [
        "#bug"
      ],
      "text": "**`response.background()` runs twice for the original streaming response: `stream_body_handler` awaits it at its tail for every response it drains; `response_handler` awaits it again on the same original after the retry loops \u2014 awaiting a Starlette `BackgroundTask` twice runs the wrapped callable twice.**\n- [ ] Continuation responses are spared \u2014 only `stream_body_handler` touches those.\n- [ ] Not verified: pipe functions that set their own background task.\n- [ ] When the chat path moves: move the second call into the `CancelledError` branch, never delete it (on cancel the first call never runs)\n- [x] _1 done step archived 2026-11-03 \u2192 docs/completed-todos.md._\n\n`#bug`\n`TODO.md:L651`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 1060,
      "y": 870
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 660,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "These calls run on the task model, which operators set small, and small models restate the format most."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 661,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Worst site is RAG queries ([middleware.py:1055](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/middleware.py#L1055)): on failure it sets the entire model reply as the retrieval query, silently degrading RAG."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 662,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "(1) Set `response_format` on the task calls \u2014 `utils/payload.py:346-353` already converts it to Ollama's `format`, and no task call sets it. A behaviour change: one at a time, fixture first (the freeze lifted 2026-08-08)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 663,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "(2) One parser as the floor in a new `utils/llm_json.py` for providers that ignore it \u2014 strip fences, try the whole string, scan for balanced objects. New file, moves no citation; can land any time."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 664,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "(3) Drop the example object from the template. A behaviour change: one at a time, fixture first (the freeze lifted 2026-08-08)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 665,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Trap: a shared helper is NOT the fix \u2014 in the restated-format case both objects are valid JSON and both carry the key, so no parser can tell them apart."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 666,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The six sites, consolidated 2026-08-08 into one `slice_json_object` helper, behaviour byte-identical (lines restated 2026-10-05):"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 667,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[808](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/middleware.py#L808) tool calling"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 668,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[968](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/middleware.py#L968) image prompt"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 669,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[1055](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/middleware.py#L1055) RAG queries"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 670,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[1494](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/middleware.py#L1494) follow-ups, through `run_json_task` (called at 1510)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 671,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[1554](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/middleware.py#L1554) title"
