    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 726,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Stall causes: network drop, HF outage, slow link."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 727,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "No timeout, no retry, no resumable state surfaced to the admin."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 728,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`wizard-smoke.sh` catches this externally via `INSTALL_TIMEOUT_SEC`."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 729,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Verified still unfixed 2026-08-03: no watchdog or `stalled` state in `routers/retrieval.py`."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 731,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Surface HF download progress (bytes, last-byte timestamp) to `request.app.state.MODEL_DOWNLOAD_STATUS` so the status endpoint exposes liveness."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 732,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Watchdog in `_download` (`retrieval.py`):"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 733,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "if cache size hasn't grown in N minutes (configurable, default 5), mark status=`stalled`, capture the error."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 734,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "allow retry via a re-POST to `/api/v1/retrieval/models/download`. Today `retrieval.py:455-456` answers \"Download already in progress\" while status reads `downloading`; the watchdog must move it off that value first."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 735,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Surface stalled state in the wizard UI with a retry button + \"check your connection\" hint."
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "8ca5dada2993087c",
      "line_num": 725,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [
        "#bug"
      ],
      "text": "**AI Engine Wizard Embedding Download Has No Stall Watchdog: when the embedding model fetch from HuggingFace stalls, the wizard sits in `embedding=downloading` indefinitely \u2014 a real user has no signal except an idle spinner.**\n- [ ] Stall causes: network drop, HF outage, slow link.\n- [ ] No timeout, no retry, no resumable state surfaced to the admin.\n- [ ] `wizard-smoke.sh` catches this externally via `INSTALL_TIMEOUT_SEC`.\n- [ ] Verified still unfixed 2026-08-03: no watchdog or `stalled` state in `routers/retrieval.py`.\n- [ ] Surface HF download progress (bytes, last-byte timestamp) to `request.app.state.MODEL_DOWNLOAD_STATUS` so the status endpoint exposes liveness.\n- [ ] Watchdog in `_download` (`retrieval.py`):\n- [ ] if cache size hasn't grown in N minutes (configurable, default 5), mark status=`stalled`, capture the error.\n- [ ] allow retry via a re-POST to `/api/v1/retrieval/models/download`. Today `retrieval.py:455-456` answers \"Download already in progress\" while status reads `downloading`; the watchdog must move it off that value first.\n- [ ] Surface stalled state in the wizard UI with a retry button + \"check your connection\" hint.\n\n`#bug`\n`TODO.md:L725`",
      "type": "text",
